Third-party components

This repository contains, or is built against, third-party software that
stays under its own licence. Nothing above limits the rights those licences
give you.

- FFmpeg 8.0.1. third_party/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-8.0.1.tar.xz is the unmodified
  upstream source. scripts/build_ffmpeg_lgpl.sh builds it with --disable-gpl
  --disable-nonfree --disable-version3 and without libx264 or libx265, so the
  resulting libraries are under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
  version 2.1 or later (third_party/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1).
- LAME (libmp3lame), linked by that build for MP3 export: GNU Library General
  Public License, version 2 or later (third_party/lame/COPYING). Not in this
  repository; the build copies the Homebrew library.
- whisper.cpp and the Whisper model weights: MIT. Not included; whisper-cli
  comes from Homebrew and the model is downloaded on first use.
- SigLIP-2 model weights (google/siglip2-base-patch16-256): Apache 2.0. Not
  included; downloaded from Hugging Face on first use.
- Silero VAD: MIT. ChromaDB, Transformers and sentence-transformers:
  Apache 2.0. PyTorch: BSD-style. Tauri: MIT or Apache 2.0.
- pillow-heif: BSD-3-Clause source, but its macOS binary wheels bundle
  libheif and libde265 (LGPL 3) and x265 (GPL 2). See third_party/NOTICE.md
  before building an app bundle.
- Inter, Inter Tight and JetBrains Mono (app/fonts/): SIL Open Font License
  1.1. The licence texts are next to the fonts, in app/fonts/LICENSE-*.txt.
- All other dependencies are declared in api/pyproject.toml,
  service_pipeline/pyproject.toml and tauri/src-tauri/Cargo.toml, each under
  its own licence.

third_party/NOTICE.md explains how the LGPL obligations would be met in a
built app bundle. No binary has been distributed from this repository. Demo
media fetched by the scripts under demo/ is not part of this repository and
keeps its original licence; sources and licences are listed in the README
next to each download script.
